    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0653" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-14T18:00:00+08:00">December 14,
                            1948—6 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 15—12:41 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>539. Director Chin Feng-chuan [of] North Chinese Bandit Suppression Headquarters
                    (see telegram 533, December 13) told me that Communists in east Hopei number
                    about 250,000 troops plus 2 columns commanded by Li Yun-chang. These exclusive
                    [of] local forces Nieh Jung-chen,<anchor n="14" xml:id="d531-f1"/> Chin reported
                    Lianghsiang and Fangshan <pb facs="0654" n="644" xml:id="pg644"/> southwest
                    Tungchow, east Chingho and Shaho northwest still held, Peiping safe for present.
                    He confirmed intentions defend Peiping but present problems were food supply and
                    manpower.</p>
                <p>Pessimistic view expressed regarding fighting Pengpu front.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking 796, Tientsin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d531-f1" n="14" xml:id="d531-f1-content">
                <p>Communist commander of the North China military area.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
